WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.040
"Do the Health Impacts of Ultra-Processed Foods
Apply to Plant-Based Meats?"

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.520
In two Harvard cohorts,
researchers followed

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.240
about a hundred thousand men
and women for decades,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.480
and found that high consumption
of ultra-processed foods

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.560
is associated
with dying earlier,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.200
which provides support
for limiting consumption

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.040
of certain types
of ultra-processed foods

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.720
for long term health.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.280
In particular, processed
meat, poultry, seafood,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.200
which generally showed
the strongest

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.720
and most consistent associations
with mortality.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.520
So here, the negative,
life-shortening effects

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.400
of ultra-processed foods
was really mostly

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.640
talking about the negative,
life-shortening effects

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.880
of processed meats like burgers,

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.440
chicken nuggets,
and fish sticks.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.000
But the association between
more ultra-processed foods

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.840
and higher mortality
appears to be present

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.880
even among vegetarians.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.080
Yes, plant-based diets,
which reduce or avoid eggs,

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.520
dairy, fish, and other meats,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.120
have been linked
to a reduced risk

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.640
of various chronic diseases,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.160
including our leading killer,
cardiovascular disease.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.680
But that doesn’t mean you can
live off vegan doughnuts.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.480
Non-ultra-processed plant foods
like fruits and vegetables

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.320
are associated with lower risk
of disease,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.240
but ultra-processed foods
like Oreos and Mountain Dew

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.560
are associated
with higher risks.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.480
So, dietary guidelines
shouldn’t just tell people

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.800
to cut down on meat
and other animal-sourced foods,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.960
but also to cut down on junk.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.720
No big surprise,

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.640
but this is how
the paper was reported on:

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.760
"The hidden health hazards
of vegan sausages."

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.440
"Vegan fake meats are linked
to increase in heart deaths."

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.080
What? If you look at the study,

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.440
meat alternatives only made up
0.2% of their diet.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.520
39.4% of their diet
was composed

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.040
of ultra-processed plant foods,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.840
but only about one 500th
of their intake

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.360
was meat alternatives.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.120
The study participants were
eating 30 times more pastries.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.040
Aren’t those
more likely to be the culprit

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.880
in the relationship
between ultra-processed foods

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.240
and disease?

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.960
14 times more French fries
and candy.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.680
Even 4 times more vodka
and other hard liquor.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.400
But apparently, there’s not
a lot of click-bait to be had

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.360
telling people not to eat
vodka and cream puffs.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.000
If you really wanted to see
if meat alternatives

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:14.880
were an issue,

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.960
you’d have to run
more granular studies

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.280
that separate out
meat alternatives for analysis.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.200
This study on obesity
had an eclectic category

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.680
of ultra-processed
"fruits and vegetables"

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.960
that included meat alternatives
along with powdered soup

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.600
and fruit compote,
and there was no tie to obesity.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.160
The culprits were mostly soda,
ice cream, mayonnaise,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.160
baloney, fish sticks,
and the like.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.160
But ideally, we’d have
a study big enough

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.360
to completely separate out
plant-based meat.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.720
If only there were some
epic study.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.280
And indeed, here it is,
the EPIC study.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.960
More than a quarter million
people were followed

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.400
for more than a decade.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.200
Yes, higher consumption
of ultra-processed foods

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.640
increases the risk of cancer

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.960
and cardiometabolic
multimorbidity,

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.840
like cardiovascular disease
and diabetes.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:06.960
Yes, but which
ultra-processed foods?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.680
It’s the animal-based
ultra-processed foods

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.000
like processed meat
and soda.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.960
No associated risk
with ultra-processed breads

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.000
and cereals or plant-based meat.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.600
And when it comes to diabetes,
plant-based meats and milks

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.040
appeared to cut the risk
of developing diabetes in half.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.640
Animal-based products
were associated

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.400
with more than twice the risk.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.400
Plant-based alternatives
were associated

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.560
with less than half.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.360
The authors concluded
that higher consumption

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.120
of ultra-processed foods
may increase

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.120
the risk of cancer
and other diseases,

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.320
but their data really only show
that the consumption of foods

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.360
of animal origin and soft drinks
is associated with such a risk,

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.360
which is like, duh.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.120
Indeed, if you go back
and exclude

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.520
the animal-based foods
and sodas,

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.600
the relationship between
ultra-processed foods

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.200
and these multiple diseases
disappears.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.360
So, the only
ultra-processed food

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.800
that appears
to be killing people is meat.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.320
In that case,
instead of being a contributor,

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.520
plant-based meats
may be the solution

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.280
to the ultra-processed foods
problem.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.280
The only other
ultra-processed study

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.520
that separated out
plant-based meats

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.360
looked at telomere length,

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.080
which is used
to measure cellular aging.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.160
Their study found
that a higher consumption

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.640
of total ultra-processed foods
was associated

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.240
with a shorter telomere length,

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.280
which is a sign
of accelerated aging.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.680
However, some subclasses
may be associated

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.440
with longer telomere length,
suggesting slower aging.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.960
And the class
of foods associated

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.800
with the longest telomeres?

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.320
Vegetarian alternatives,
plant-based meat.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.960
There have been
other population studies

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.080
on plant-based meats.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.760
This one found
that those who ate

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.680
plant-based meat daily
appeared to cut their risk

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.960
of hip fracture in half

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.280
compared to those eating
it less than once a week.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.120
Schoolchildren who eat
plant-based meats

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.120
appear to have half the odds
of being overweight

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.960
compared to those
eating regular meat.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.040
And girls who eat more meat

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.040
start their periods
at an earlier age,

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.920
which may help explain
why childhood meat consumption

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.680
is linked to breast cancer
later in life,

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.600
since the earlier
you start your period,

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.840
the higher your lifetime risk.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.000
In contrast,
those eating plant-based meats

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.560
appear able to delay
the onset of menstruation

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.400
by nine months.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.480
But observational studies
like these

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.080
can’t ever prove
cause-and-effect.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.960
For that, you need
interventional trials.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.360
There have been 10
published up through 2023

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.440
and a few more since then.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.320
I did a video on the Stanford
SWAP-MEAT study

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.960
that showed swapping out
a few servings a day of meat

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.560
for plant-based
meat alternatives

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.520
for two months significantly
decreased circulating levels

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.160
of the microbiome toxin TMAO,

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.200
as well as lowered
LDL cholesterol and body weight.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.080
But there have been about
a dozen other studies,

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.600
including this four-year long
randomized clinical trial

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.760
in which people with diabetes
and ailing kidneys

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.480
were randomized to replace
half their animal protein intake

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.200
with an ultra-processed
plant-based meat replacement

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.040
called TVP.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.280
The researchers saw
significant improvements

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.200
in blood sugar control,
cholesterol,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.880
triglycerides, inflammation,

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.840
and significant improvements
in their kidney function.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.000
I’ll cover all these studies.
Stay tuned.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.280
And, if you don't want to wait,

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.520
I've got a new book out
that covers them all,

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.800
a short peer-reviewed paper that's
free to download at see.nf/ultra,

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:31.279
and a CME-approved webinar
you can watch as well.

